{"id":"pattern-example-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Example: Use mock factories for all test data instead of manual mock objects with 'as Type' assertions.","recommendation":"Create centralized mock factory functions (createMockUser, createMockOrg, etc.) and import them in tests.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"documentation","reference":"Testing guide","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["testing","mocks","factories"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.test.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-pragma-no-cover-subprocess-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Async subprocess/stdio functions (like MCP's stdio_client) cannot be unit-tested without a live external process. Mark them with `# pragma: no cover` on the def line. Test coverage is achieved on the public synchronous wrapper by mocking concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor.","recommendation":"Structure: async def _fn(...): # pragma: no cover (does real I/O) + def public_fn(...): with ThreadPoolExecutor() as ex: return ex.submit(_run).result(). Tests mock ThreadPoolExecutor to control the return value without spawning subprocesses.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"feature/003-inline-pr-comments — backend/mcp/client.py + backend/tests/mcp/test_client.py","date":"2026-06-16"}],"tags":["testing","coverage","pragma","subprocess","mcp","python"],"affectedFiles":["backend/mcp/**/*.py","backend/tests/mcp/**/*.py"],"affectedServices":["GitHubMCPClient"],"createdAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-git-recover-deleted-files-001","type":"pattern","fact":"When a commit accidentally deletes implementation files, all content is recoverable from git history using `git show <sha>:<path>` — even if the files are no longer present on any branch.","recommendation":"Run `git log --all --diff-filter=D --name-only --oneline` to find the commit that deleted files, then `git show <sha>:<path>` to retrieve each file's last content before deletion. Pipe to a new file or recreate directly.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"feature/003-inline-pr-comments — commit 43b4008 wiped github implementation files","date":"2026-06-16"}],"tags":["git","recovery","deleted-files","workflow"],"affectedFiles":[],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-sqlalchemy-001","type":"pattern","fact":"SQLAlchemy provider classes should accept an optional session_factory parameter (defaulting to SessionLocal) to enable unit testing without a live database.","recommendation":"Define __init__(self, session_factory=None) and assign self._session_factory = session_factory or SessionLocal. Tests pass lambda: mock_session; production uses the real SessionLocal.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"human","reference":"feature/004-provider-selection session","date":"2026-06-17"}],"tags":["sqlalchemy","testing","dependency-injection","python"],"affectedFiles":["backend/providers/data_source/**/*.py","backend/tests/providers/**/*.py"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-lazy-import-001","type":"pattern","fact":"In plugin_registry.py, provider classes that could create circular imports should be imported lazily inside the if-branch that instantiates them, not at module top-level.","recommendation":"Use local imports inside factory branches: `if provider == 'cloudwatch': from backend.providers.log_backend.cloudwatch import CloudWatchLogBackend; return CloudWatchLogBackend()`. Top-level imports are fine for providers with no circular risk.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"human","reference":"feature/004-provider-selection session","date":"2026-06-17"}],"tags":["python","imports","circular-imports","plugin-registry"],"affectedFiles":["backend/plugin_registry.py"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
